<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64825" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάλη</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], ἡ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>arm-pit</i>, almost confined to the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ μάλης</span>
			<i>under the arm</i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				76
			</span></i>), esp. as the place for carrying concealed weapons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξιφίδια ὑπὸ μ. ἔχοντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					2.3.23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαβὼν ὑπὸ μ. ἐγχειρίδιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					469d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.Euerg.
				3
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόρυ δῆθ᾽ ὑπὸ μ. ἥκεις
			ἔχων</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				985
			</span></i>: Com., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαγύνιον ἔχων ὑπὸ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diph.
					3.3
				</span></i>
			; also, of fighting-quails, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ μ. λαβεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					789c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρύπτειν ὑπὸ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Ind.</u>
					23
				</span></i>
			 (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ μάλην ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Gall.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τὴν μ. πατάξας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					202
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ τὴν μ. ἢ ὑπὸ
			ζώνην</span>, of a horse, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hippiatr.</u>
				26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>underhand, secretly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ὑπὸ μ. ἡ πρόκλησις γέγονεν, ἀλλ᾽
					ἐν τῇ ἀγορᾷ μέσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					29.12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				46.23
			</span></i>.</div>
